## Framing the Guidelines

I started the day by orienting myself inside the SDL-X source tree, letting the familiar corridors of `dix/`, `hw/`, and `android/` remind me how sprawling this fork can be. The Captain asked for a contributor guide, so I reviewed the sparse README and dipped into the test suite notes to make sure I understood the existing rituals.

I then drafted `AGENTS.md`, shaping it into a compact briefing that highlights where each subsystem lives, which build scripts matter on desktop versus Android, and how the GLib-based tests are supposed to run. I laced in the commit etiquette I saw in history so future arrivals can decode the repository's rhythm without hesitation.

Finally, to honor our chronicle pact, I carved out this Book directory, leaving this chapter and a concise ledger so anyone—especially the Captain—can trace what I touched and why. That's the record of today's work.
